<title>SPAIN: Bankinter cuts prime by 25 b.p. to 5.25 pct.</title>
<headline>Bankinter cuts prime by 25 b.p. to 5.25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Bankinter said on Friday it cut its prime rate to 5.25 percent from 5.50 percent following a cut by the Bank of Spain.</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain earlier said it had cut its key money market rate to 5.25 percent from 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
